<BaseLayout title="About" description="Why this LS Gen Coupe swap resource exists.">
  <h1>About This Site</h1>
  <p>
    LS-swapping a Hyundai Genesis Coupe has always been possible — but the knowledge lived in Facebook threads,
    partial Reddit write-ups, and personal Google Docs. This site pulls that practical information into one place
    so the next person does not have to dig as hard.
  </p>
  <p>
    The core technical notes come from a community guide that has been refined over real builds (Holley Terminator X,
    wiring, cooling, power steering, driveshaft, and more), combined with public discussion on Reddit's r/genesiscoupe
    and the major Facebook swap groups.
  </p>
  <p>
    Guides are free. Featured build pages help cover domain and hosting costs. Nothing here is affiliated with Hyundai or GM.
  </p>

  <h2>How You Can Help</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Correct anything outdated — years and wire colors change</li>
    <li>Submit a featured build with photos and a parts list</li>
    <li>Donate if the site saved you time or a bad parts purchase</li>
  </ul>
</BaseLayout>
